    "step_exclude_fields_reason": "sts2-rs-rggx: per-step shape lock \u2014 Python MT vs Rust Xoshiro256++ roll different intent branches across the 10-turn walk, so damage-derived fields (hp/block/is_alive/powers) and post-game-over freeze fields (/round, player.energy, player.max_energy) are excluded. Only structural shape (type tag, top-level keys, enemy id/max_hp, pile counts, player/max_hp) is byte-locked.\n\n2026-05-28 follow-up: /hand was added to the exclude set for THIS fixture (and only this one) because C# MechaKnight.AfterAddedToRoom calls `CardPileCmd.AddToCombatAndPreview<Burn>(targets, PileType.Hand, 4)` (MegaCrit.Sts2.Core.Models.Monsters/MechaKnight.cs:72-135) and the Rust port now mirrors that, so the player's hand carries 4 Burn status cards from spawn onward. The fixture was authored against an older Rust pin (bc04805d, see metadata.rust_pin) that predated this wiring; its expected hand state is stale. The other 8 act23 fixtures keep their /hand byte-lock."
